.TH BLIND-PEW 1 "November 2026" "Blind Pew 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
blind-pew \- offline transliteration and input-source switching
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B blind-pew
.RI [ setup | doctor | list | toggle | disconnect ]
.br
.B blind-pew convert
.RB [ --profile " PROFILE" ]
.RB [ --reverse ]
.br
.B blind-pew
.RB [ --version | --help ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Blind Pew provides IBus transliteration for Belarusian, Ukrainian, Lithuanian,
Georgian, Armenian, Russian and Hebrew on Debian/Ubuntu with GNOME or Xfce.
The settings window selects a profile and QWERTY or QWERTZ base.
F12 and vertical scrolling over the tray toggle the selected transliteration
and the previous ordinary input source while the application is running.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B setup
Open settings. This is also the default when no command is supplied.
.TP
.B doctor
Report the desktop environment and IBus engine registration; return a nonzero
status when IBus or expected engines are unavailable.
.TP
.B list
List the installed program's available engine IDs and profile names.
.TP
.B toggle
Send a toggle action to the running settings application.
.TP
.B disconnect
Remove Blind Pew sources and restore saved input/shortcut settings.
Use an ordinary input source and quit the application before uninstalling.
.TP
.B convert
Read standard input and write transliterated text to standard output.
This command works without a graphical session or an IBus daemon.
.TP
.BI "\-\-profile " PROFILE
Converter profile: be, ua, li, ge, am, ru, rude or il. Default: ru.
.TP
.B \-\-reverse
Convert the selected script to Latin characters.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/blind-pew/settings.json
Preferences and saved desktop settings. An absolute XDG_CONFIG_HOME overrides
~/.config. Typed text is not stored in this file.
.TP
.I /usr/share/doc/blind-pew/
README translations, licensing notices, test scope and release documentation.
.SH NOTES
The application uses system IBus modules, including ibus-gtk4 for GTK4 clients.
GNOME requires the supplied Blind Pew Integration extension and an AppIndicator
extension for the tray. Xfce requires a tray panel item.
Password, PIN and Private fields bypass conversion when the client marks them.
Blind Pew does not operate in a TTY or at the login screen.
